Optional server-side price filtering and sorting
================================================

Apply inside `showProducts()` and `showProductsWithoutAuth()` in
app/Http/Controllers/Application/Product/ProductController.php, immediately
before the existing `// Default order` line.

All three parameters are optional, so existing mobile-app requests that do not
send them behave exactly as they do today.

--- ProductController.php
+++ ProductController.php
@@ existing filters (sellerID) @@
             if ($request->filled('sellerID')) {
                 $query->where('userID', $request->sellerID);
             }
 
+            // Price range (optional; added for the web client's filters).
+            if ($request->filled('minPrice') && is_numeric($request->minPrice)) {
+                $query->where('price', '>=', (float) $request->minPrice);
+            }
+            if ($request->filled('maxPrice') && is_numeric($request->maxPrice)) {
+                $query->where('price', '<=', (float) $request->maxPrice);
+            }
+
+            // Condition (1 = new, 2 = used).
+            if ($request->filled('condition')) {
+                $query->where('condition', (int) $request->condition);
+            }
+
+            // Sorting (optional). Unknown values fall through to the default.
+            $sortBy = (string) $request->input('sortBy', '');
+            $sorted = true;
+            switch ($sortBy) {
+                case 'price_asc':
+                    $query->orderBy('price', 'asc');
+                    break;
+                case 'price_desc':
+                    $query->orderBy('price', 'desc');
+                    break;
+                case 'oldest':
+                    $query->orderBy('created_at', 'asc');
+                    break;
+                case 'newest':
+                    $query->orderBy('created_at', 'desc');
+                    break;
+                default:
+                    $sorted = false;
+            }
+
             // Default order
-            $query->orderBy('created_at', 'desc');
+            if (!$sorted) {
+                $query->orderBy('created_at', 'desc');
+            }

Recommended indexes (MySQL) for these filters at scale:

    ALTER TABLE products ADD INDEX products_status_created_idx (status, created_at);
    ALTER TABLE products ADD INDEX products_category_idx (categoryID, status);
    ALTER TABLE products ADD INDEX products_subcategory_idx (subCategoryID, status);
    ALTER TABLE products ADD INDEX products_user_idx (userID, status);
    ALTER TABLE products ADD INDEX products_price_idx (price);
